HALTED BY OPERATOR AT 5/126 — STRUCTURAL: HIDDEN GATE CANNOT RUN UNDER
isolation=container, SO acceptance.result IS `error` FOR EVERY RUN
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Kill switch armed 2026-08-17T16:32:10Z (touch results/screening-batch1/HALT).
Driver stopped cleanly before plan index 6; collector backfill completed.
Runs completed: 5 of 126.  Product-A authoritative spend: $1.8634 of the $75 cap.

Finding (mechanical, reproduced, not inferred):
  All 5 runs record acceptance.result = "error" with
  gate_checks.hidden = {status: awaiting_human, hash: null, version: null},
  while all 7 public checks (G0,P1..P6) pass.

Cause:
  - The batch runs ISOLATION="container", so run.py:684 dispatches the gate to
    container_gate() (run.py:564-597) instead of the host gate real_gate().
  - container_gate() mounts only run_dir -> /out and the agent volume -> the
    subject repo (run.py:582-584). It does NOT mount the sealed hidden set.
  - .dockerignore excludes **/hidden/ from every image by design, and its own
    comment states the intent: "The runtime gate needs only gate/ + tests/
    (+ MOUNTED hidden/)". The mount was never implemented.
  - Verified directly: /lab/tasks/pilot-realworld/hidden does not exist in
    lab-subject/pilot-realworld-draft-articles:30b68e1e8814.
  - check-hidden.sh therefore finds no sealed tests, writes awaiting_human and
    exits 2; _gate_verdict() maps hid_rc==2 to "error" (run.py:528-529).

Scope: deterministic and isolation-dependent, not task-dependent. It applies to
all 126 runs and to every task in the roster, including the six W-tasks whose
sealed artifacts were frozen this morning.

Corroborating history (results/smoke-screening/): the 2 runs whose agent leg ran
on the HOST are accepted/hidden=pass; all 9 containerized runs are
error/awaiting_human. The signal was present in the smoke evidence and was not
caught before launch.

NOT a fabrication or a measurement gap: the telemetry for these 5 runs is real
and authoritative (validate: PASS on all five). What is missing is the DEPENDENT
VARIABLE — no run in this configuration can be scored accepted or rejected.

Disposition: awaiting human decision. No runner change made (standing "no runner
change tonight"). The 5 completed runs stay on disk as a partial, honestly
labelled record; they are NOT a screening result.

